### Path Anchoring Rules

| File | Location | Paths relative to |
|---|---|---|
| `orval.config.ts` | `/frontend` | `/frontend` |
| `angular.json` | `/frontend` | `/frontend` |
| `tsconfig.json` | `/frontend` | `/frontend` |
| `dotnet ef` commands | `/backend` | `/backend` |

### CI Path Rules

- Backend CI (`backend.yml`) runs from `/backend` — does NOT touch `/frontend`
- Frontend CI (`frontend.yml`) runs from `/frontend` — does NOT touch `/backend`
- `swagger.json` diff check: backend CI publishes swagger artifact; frontend CI downloads it and runs `npx orval --check`
- NEVER use repo-root-relative paths inside `orval.config.ts` or `angular.json`

---

## Architecture Principles

- Clean Architecture (Controller -> Handler -> Repository)
- CQRS via MediatR: Commands for writes, Queries for reads
- Controllers are thin: they only dispatch to MediatR and return HTTP responses
- ALL business logic lives in Application layer as MediatR Command/Query handlers
- Domain-driven design mindset
- Microservices-ready (loose coupling, high cohesion)
- Avoid premature distribution (start modular, evolve later)

---

## Domain Language (STRICT — use ONLY these terms)

| Term | Never use |
|---|---|
| `User` | client, account holder |
| `Transaction` | payment, expense, entry |
| `Category` | tag, label |
| `Merchant` | vendor, store |
| `Classification` | tag, label, category AI result |
| `AmountCents` (long) | amount, value (without the Cents suffix) |
| `NormalizedAmountCents` (long) | normalized amount, USD amount |

Rules:
- `AmountCents` is always `long` — raw amount in the smallest currency unit
- `NormalizedAmountCents` is always `long` — always in USD for cross-currency comparison
- Currency code is always required alongside any amount
- NEVER use `decimal`, `double`, `float`, or `int` for money anywhere

