## Backend — Project Structure and Layer Rules

### Solution Layout (STRICT)

```
/FinanceCore.sln

/src
  /FinanceCore.Api               <- Controllers, middleware, Swagger, Program.cs
  /FinanceCore.Application       <- Commands, Queries, Handlers, DTOs, Validators
  /FinanceCore.Domain            <- Domain models, interfaces (IRepository), enums, value objects
  /FinanceCore.Infrastructure    <- EF Core DbContext, Repository implementations, migrations

/tests
  /FinanceCore.UnitTests         <- Handler-layer unit tests (xUnit + Moq + FluentAssertions)
  /FinanceCore.IntegrationTests  <- Controller-level integration tests (WebApplicationFactory)
```

### Project Dependency Rules (STRICT)

```
Api -> Application -> Domain
Infrastructure -> Application -> Domain
```

- `Api` depends on `Application` only (dispatches MediatR requests)
- `Application` depends on `Domain` (uses domain models and IRepository interfaces)
- `Infrastructure` depends on `Application` and `Domain` (implements interfaces)
- `Domain` has NO dependencies on other projects
- `Api` MUST NOT reference `Infrastructure` directly (only via DI registration)
- `FinanceCore.Domain.csproj` MUST NOT list `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore` as a PackageReference

