## Domain Model (STRICT)

### Entity Design

```csharp
public sealed class Transaction
{
    public Guid Id { get; private set; }
    public Guid UserId { get; private set; }
    public Money Amount { get; private set; }
    public TransactionType Type { get; private set; }
    public Guid? MerchantId { get; private set; }
    public Guid? CategoryId { get; private set; }
    public DateTimeOffset OccurredAt { get; private set; }
    public string? Description { get; private set; }

    private Transaction() { }  // Required by EF Core

    public static Transaction Create(
        Guid userId, Money amount, TransactionType type,
        DateTimeOffset occurredAt, string? description,
        Guid? merchantId = null, Guid? categoryId = null)
    {
        if (occurredAt.Offset != TimeSpan.Zero)
            throw new DomainException("OccurredAt must be UTC (offset must be zero).");

        return new Transaction
        {
            Id = Guid.NewGuid(),
            UserId = userId, Amount = amount, Type = type,
            OccurredAt = occurredAt, Description = description,
            MerchantId = merchantId, CategoryId = categoryId,
        };
    }
}
```

### Money Value Object (CRITICAL)

Money is ALWAYS stored as `long` cents + currency code.
Never use `decimal`, `double`, `float`, or `int`.

```csharp
// Domain/Shared/ValueObjects/Money.cs
public sealed record Money
{
    public long AmountCents { get; }
    public long NormalizedAmountCents { get; }  // always USD
    public string Currency { get; }

    public Money(long amountCents, string currency, long? normalizedAmountCents = null)
    {
        if (amountCents < 0)
            throw new DomainException("Amount cannot be negative.");
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(currency))
            throw new DomainException("Currency is required.");
        if (currency.Length != 3)
            throw new DomainException("Currency must be a 3-letter ISO 4217 code.");

        AmountCents = amountCents;
        Currency = currency.ToUpperInvariant();
        NormalizedAmountCents = normalizedAmountCents ?? amountCents;
    }
}
```

EF Core configuration:
```csharp
builder.OwnsOne(t => t.Amount, money =>
{
    money.Property(m => m.AmountCents).HasColumnName("amount_cents").IsRequired();
    money.Property(m => m.NormalizedAmountCents).HasColumnName("normalized_amount_cents").IsRequired();
    money.Property(m => m.Currency).HasColumnName("currency").HasMaxLength(3).IsRequired();
});
```

---

## Date and Time (CRITICAL)

All timestamps use `DateTimeOffset`. All values stored and transmitted in UTC.

```csharp
// Enforce in every factory method:
if (occurredAt.Offset != TimeSpan.Zero)
    throw new DomainException("OccurredAt must be UTC (offset must be zero).");
```

### DateTimeOffsetUtcConverter (REQUIRED — implement exactly)

```csharp
// Infrastructure/Persistence/Converters/DateTimeOffsetUtcConverter.cs
public sealed class DateTimeOffsetUtcConverter : ValueConverter<DateTimeOffset, DateTimeOffset>
{
    public DateTimeOffsetUtcConverter()
        : base(
            d => d.ToUniversalTime(),
            d => new DateTimeOffset(d.Ticks, TimeSpan.Zero))
    { }
}
```

Register globally in FinanceCoreDbContext:
```csharp
protected override void ConfigureConventions(ModelConfigurationBuilder configurationBuilder)
{
    configurationBuilder.Properties<DateTimeOffset>()
        .HaveConversion<DateTimeOffsetUtcConverter>();
}
```

### JSON serialization (single block in Program.cs)

```csharp
builder.Services.AddControllers().AddJsonOptions(options =>
{
    options.JsonSerializerOptions.PropertyNamingPolicy   = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase;
    options.JsonSerializerOptions.DefaultIgnoreCondition = JsonIgnoreCondition.WhenWritingNull;
    options.JsonSerializerOptions.Converters.Add(new JsonStringEnumConverter());
});
```

CRITICAL: JsonStringEnumConverter makes enums serialize as strings ("Income" not 1).
Swashbuckle reads this and emits string enums in OpenAPI.
orval generates TypeScript string literal unions (e.g. 'Income' | 'Expense').
Do NOT omit this converter.

### End-to-End Date Pipeline

```
DB: timestamptz (always UTC)
  -> Npgsql + DateTimeOffsetUtcConverter
Domain: DateTimeOffset (UTC, Offset == Zero enforced)
  -> TransactionMapper.ToDto()
DTO: DateTimeOffset OccurredAt
  -> System.Text.Json -> "2024-03-15T10:30:00+00:00"
  -> OpenAPI (format: date-time) -> orval date transformer
TypeScript: occurredAt: Date
  -> DateFormatPipe
UI: "Mar 15, 2024, 10:30 AM"
```

### orval date transformer (REQUIRED)

```typescript
// frontend/src/app/core/orval-date.transformer.ts
import type { OutputTransformer } from 'orval';

const transformer: OutputTransformer = (output) => ({
  ...output,
  schemas: output.schemas.map(schema => ({
    ...schema,
    model: schema.model.replace(
      /(\w+\s*:\s*)string(.*\/\/ date-time)/g,
      '$1Date$2'
    ),
  })),
});

export default transformer;
```

After every `npx orval` run, verify that `occurredAt` in generated models is `Date`, not `string`.
If the pattern breaks, pin the orval minor version and open a task.

### Frontend date display

```typescript
// shared/pipes/date-format.pipe.ts
@Pipe({ name: 'dateFormat', standalone: true })
export class DateFormatPipe implements PipeTransform {
  transform(value: Date | string | null | undefined, format: 'short' | 'long' = 'short'): string {
    if (!value) return '-';
    const date = value instanceof Date ? value : new Date(value);
    return date.toLocaleString('en-US', {
      dateStyle: format === 'long' ? 'long' : 'medium',
      timeStyle: 'short',
      timeZone: 'UTC',
    });
  }
}
```

Rules:
- NEVER `new Date()` on a raw API string outside of DateFormatPipe or a facade
- NEVER assume local timezone — always pass `timeZone: 'UTC'`

---

## DTO vs. Domain Model (STRICT)

| Type | Location | Exposed via API? |
|---|---|---|
| Domain model (Transaction) | Domain | NEVER |
| DTO (TransactionDto) | Application | YES |
| EF Configuration | Infrastructure | NEVER |

- Domain model -> DTO: in the Handler via an explicit mapper class
- DTO/command -> domain model: via domain factory methods (Transaction.Create(...))
- DO NOT use AutoMapper — explicit typed mapper methods only

---

## Coding Conventions (STRICT)

- NO `var` when the type is not obvious from the right-hand side
- NO `dynamic`
- NO static classes (use DI)
- NO service locator pattern
- Strong typing everywhere; all code in English
- Functions <= 40 lines, single responsibility
- Files <= 300 lines — split by command/query slice when nearing the limit
- Explicit naming (no `data`, `info`, `helper`)

### Layer Responsibilities

- Controller -> dispatch MediatR + return HTTP response
- Handler -> business logic + ownership checks + SaveChanges
- Repository -> data access only, never calls SaveChanges
- Domain model -> invariants + behavior

### Naming — C#

- Classes, Methods, Properties, Interfaces, Enums, Constants -> PascalCase
- Interfaces -> I prefix
- Local variables, parameters -> camelCase
- Private fields -> _camelCase

### Naming — TypeScript

- Variables, Functions -> camelCase
- Classes, Interfaces -> PascalCase
- Constants -> UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Files -> kebab-case
- NEVER `any` — use explicit types or `unknown` with type guards

---

## CancellationToken Forwarding (STRICT)

Every public async method from Controller through Repository must accept and forward
CancellationToken. No exceptions — including SaveChangesAsync.

```
Controller action (bound by Kestrel)
  -> mediator.Send(request, cancellationToken)
    -> Handler.Handle(request, cancellationToken)
      -> Repository method (cancellationToken)
        -> EF Core call (.FirstOrDefaultAsync(ct), .SaveChangesAsync(ct))
```

Repository interface (canonical):
```csharp
public interface ITransactionRepository
{
    Task<Transaction?> GetByIdAsync(Guid id, CancellationToken cancellationToken);
    Task<IReadOnlyList<Transaction>> GetByUserIdAsync(Guid userId, int page, int pageSize,
                                                      CancellationToken cancellationToken);
    Task AddAsync(Transaction transaction, CancellationToken cancellationToken);
    Task UpdateAsync(Transaction transaction, CancellationToken cancellationToken);
}
```

Anti-patterns (STRICTLY FORBIDDEN):
- Any async method without CancellationToken
- CancellationToken.None passed explicitly in application code
- SaveChangesAsync() without a token

---

## Validation (STRICT)

| Layer | Tool | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Domain factory / value objects | Guard clauses | DomainException -> 400 |
| Application commands | FluentValidation | ValidationException -> 422 |
| Business rules in handlers | Result.Failure(Error.X(...)) | mapped by ToProblemResult() |

Controllers do NOT validate.

```csharp
public sealed class CreateTransactionCommandValidator
    : AbstractValidator<CreateTransactionCommand>
{
    public CreateTransactionCommandValidator()
    {
        RuleFor(x => x.UserId).NotEmpty();
        RuleFor(x => x.Amount.Value).GreaterThan(0);
        RuleFor(x => x.Amount.Currency).NotEmpty().Length(3);
        RuleFor(x => x.Type).IsInEnum();
        RuleFor(x => x.OccurredAt).NotEqual(default(DateTimeOffset));
    }
}
```

```csharp
// Program.cs
builder.Services.AddValidatorsFromAssembly(typeof(CreateTransactionCommand).Assembly);
builder.Services.AddFluentValidationAutoValidation();
```

### HTTP Status Semantics

| Situation | Status |
|---|---|
| FluentValidation failure | 422 Unprocessable Entity |
| Domain invariant violation | 400 Bad Request |
| Error.NotFound | 404 Not Found |
| Error.Forbidden | 403 Forbidden |
| Invalid/missing JWT claim | 401 Unauthorized |

All errors use RFC 7807 Problem Details.

---

## Authorization (STRICT)

- Global AuthorizeFilter on all controllers
- Ownership check in the Handler — never in Controller or Repository
- Every handler that touches a user-owned resource receives CallerId in the request object

```csharp
// Api/Shared/ApiControllerBase.cs
protected Guid GetCurrentUserId()
{
    string? sub = User.FindFirstValue(ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier);
    if (sub is null || !Guid.TryParse(sub, out Guid userId))
        throw new InvalidClaimException();
    return userId;
}
```

Verify JwtBearerOptions.MapInboundClaims = false in Program.cs and confirm the IdP
populates `sub` as a GUID string before wiring real auth.

---

## Exception Model (STRICT)

DomainException -> domain invariant violations (-> 400).
AppException subtypes -> infrastructure/auth failures only.
Business errors -> Result<T>, not exceptions.

```csharp
public sealed class DomainException : Exception
{
    public DomainException(string message) : base(message) { }
}

public abstract class AppException : Exception
{
    public int StatusCode { get; }
    public string ErrorType { get; }
    protected AppException(int statusCode, string errorType, string message)
        : base(message) { StatusCode = statusCode; ErrorType = errorType; }
}

public sealed class InvalidClaimException : AppException
{
    public InvalidClaimException()
        : base(401, "https://financecore.dev/errors/invalid-claim",
               "The JWT subject claim is missing or malformed.") { }
}
```

UnauthorizedAccessException (BCL) is NEVER thrown. Use InvalidClaimException.

### ExceptionHandlingMiddleware

```csharp
public sealed class ExceptionHandlingMiddleware
{
    private readonly RequestDelegate _next;
    private readonly ILogger<ExceptionHandlingMiddleware> _logger;

    public ExceptionHandlingMiddleware(RequestDelegate next,
                                       ILogger<ExceptionHandlingMiddleware> logger)
    { _next = next; _logger = logger; }

    public async Task InvokeAsync(HttpContext context)
    {
        try { await _next(context); }
        catch (Exception ex) { await HandleAsync(context, ex); }
    }

    private async Task HandleAsync(HttpContext context, Exception exception)
    {
        (int status, string type, string title, string? detail) = exception switch
        {
            ValidationException ve => (422,
                "https://financecore.dev/errors/validation-failed", "Validation failed",
                string.Join("; ", ve.Errors.Select(e => e.ErrorMessage))),
            DomainException de => (400,
                "https://financecore.dev/errors/domain-rule-violation", "Domain rule violation",
                de.Message),
            AppException ae => (ae.StatusCode, ae.ErrorType, ResolveTitle(ae.StatusCode), ae.Message),
            _ => (500, "https://financecore.dev/errors/internal", "Internal server error", null)
        };

        if (status == 500)
            _logger.LogError(exception, "Unhandled exception on {Path}", context.Request.Path);

        ProblemDetails problem = new()
        {
            Status = status, Type = type, Title = title, Detail = detail,
            Instance = context.Request.Path,
        };
        problem.Extensions["traceId"] = Activity.Current?.Id ?? context.TraceIdentifier;

        context.Response.StatusCode  = status;
        context.Response.ContentType = "application/problem+json";
        await context.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(problem);
    }

    private static string ResolveTitle(int status) => status switch
    {
        401 => "Unauthorized", 403 => "Forbidden", 404 => "Not found", _ => "Application error",
    };
}
```

Register in Program.cs BEFORE routing:
```csharp
app.UseMiddleware<ExceptionHandlingMiddleware>();
app.UseAuthentication();
app.UseAuthorization();
app.MapControllers();
```

---

## Data Access Strategy (STRICT)

- DbContext exists ONLY in Infrastructure
- Handlers depend on IXxxRepository and IUnitOfWork — never on DbContext
- Repositories return domain models, NOT IQueryable
- Default to AsNoTracking() for reads; tracking only on write paths
- DO NOT implement generic repositories
- SaveChangesAsync is called ONLY in the Handler

### IDbTransaction for multi-repository operations

```csharp
// Application/Shared/IDbTransaction.cs
public interface IDbTransaction : IAsyncDisposable
{
    Task CommitAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
    Task RollbackAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
}

// Application/Shared/IUnitOfWork.cs
public interface IUnitOfWork
{
    Task SaveChangesAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
    Task<IDbTransaction> BeginTransactionAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
}
```

Handler multi-repository pattern:
```csharp
await using IDbTransaction tx = await _unitOfWork.BeginTransactionAsync(cancellationToken);
try
{
    await _transactionRepository.AddAsync(transaction, cancellationToken);
    await _classificationRepository.AddAsync(classification, cancellationToken);
    await _unitOfWork.SaveChangesAsync(cancellationToken);
    await tx.CommitAsync(cancellationToken);
    return Result.Success(TransactionMapper.ToDto(transaction));
}
catch
{
    await tx.RollbackAsync(cancellationToken);
    throw;
}
```

### Migrations

```bash
# run from /backend
dotnet ef migrations add <Name> \
  --project src/FinanceCore.Infrastructure \
  --startup-project src/FinanceCore.Api

dotnet ef database update \
  --project src/FinanceCore.Infrastructure \
  --startup-project src/FinanceCore.Api
```

### Query Rules

- Avoid N+1 (use Include when needed)
- Always paginate (default pageSize = 20, max pageSize = 100; return 400 if exceeded)

---

## API Contract and Frontend Integration (STRICT)

### orval Configuration

```typescript
// frontend/orval.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from 'orval';

export default defineConfig({
  financeCore: {
    input: {
      target: process.env['SWAGGER_URL'] ?? 'http://localhost:5000/swagger/v1/swagger.json',
    },
    output: {
      target:  'src/app/api-client/finance-core.service.ts',
      schemas: 'src/app/api-client/models',
      client:  'angular',
      baseUrl: '',
      override: {
        mutator: { path: 'src/app/core/http-client.mutator.ts', name: 'customHttpClient' },
        transformer: 'src/app/core/orval-date.transformer.ts',
      },
    },
  },
});
```

```typescript
// frontend/src/app/core/http-client.mutator.ts
import { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';
import { inject } from '@angular/core';
import { environment } from '../../environments/environment';

export const customHttpClient = <T>(config: Parameters<HttpClient['request']>[0]) => {
  const http = inject(HttpClient);
  return http.request<T>({ ...config, url: `${environment.apiBaseUrl}${config.url}` });
};
```

Backend runs on http://localhost:5000 for local dev.
If switching to HTTPS (5001), update environment.ts and the orval fallback in the same commit.

### API Versioning

```
/api/v1/transactions
/api/v1/categories
/api/v1/merchants
```

Breaking changes -> new version. Never break existing contracts silently.

### Money DTO (CRITICAL)

```csharp
// Application/Shared/Dtos/MoneyDto.cs
public sealed record MoneyDto
{
    public long Value { get; init; }           // AmountCents on the wire
    public long NormalizedValue { get; init; } // NormalizedAmountCents in USD
    public string Currency { get; init; } = string.Empty;
}
```

Wire JSON:
```json
{ "amount": { "value": 5000, "normalizedValue": 5000, "currency": "USD" } }
```

```csharp
public static class MoneyMapper
{
    public static MoneyDto ToDto(Money money) => new()
    {
        Value = money.AmountCents,
        NormalizedValue = money.NormalizedAmountCents,
        Currency = money.Currency,
    };

    public static Money ToDomain(MoneyDto dto) =>
        new(dto.Value, dto.Currency, dto.NormalizedValue);
}
```

Frontend pipe:
```typescript
@Pipe({ name: 'moneyFormat', standalone: true })
export class MoneyFormatPipe implements PipeTransform {
  transform(amount: MoneyDto): string {
    return (amount.value / 100).toLocaleString('en-US', {
      style: 'currency',
      currency: amount.currency,
    });
  }
}
```

Rules:
- amount.value is cents — / 100 happens ONLY inside MoneyFormatPipe
- value is always long (TypeScript number) — never decimal or float

### Pagination Contract

```
GET /api/v1/transactions?page=1&pageSize=20
```

```json
{ "data": [...], "meta": { "page": 1, "pageSize": 20, "totalItems": 100, "totalPages": 5 } }
```

Default pageSize: 20 — Max: 100 — return 400 if exceeded.

