## Angular Frontend Architecture (STRICT)

### Bootstrap Strategy

Standalone components + bootstrapApplication. NgModules are FORBIDDEN.

```typescript
export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {
  providers: [
    provideRouter(routes),
    provideHttpClient(withInterceptors([authInterceptor, errorInterceptor])),
  ],
};
```

### inject() Function (REQUIRED — not constructor injection)

```typescript
// CORRECT
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class TransactionFacadeService {
  private readonly api = inject(FinanceCoreService);
  private readonly router = inject(Router);
}

// FORBIDDEN
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class TransactionFacadeService {
  constructor(private readonly api: FinanceCoreService) {}
}
```

### Functional Interceptors (REQUIRED)

```typescript
export const authInterceptor: HttpInterceptorFn = (req, next) => {
  const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
  const authReq = token
    ? req.clone({ setHeaders: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } })
    : req;
  return next(authReq);
};
```

localStorage for the token is the accepted tradeoff. Do not change without an explicit decision.

### Lazy Routes

```typescript
{
  path: 'transactions',
  loadComponent: () =>
    import('./features/transactions/pages/transaction-list.page')
      .then(m => m.TransactionListPage),
}
```

### Folder Structure

```
/src/app
  /core
    /interceptors
      auth.interceptor.ts
      error.interceptor.ts
    /guards
      auth.guard.ts
  /shared
    /components
    /pipes
      money-format.pipe.ts
      date-format.pipe.ts
    /models
      problem-details.model.ts
  /features
    /transactions
      /components
      /pages
        transaction-list.page.ts
        transaction-detail.page.ts
      transaction.routes.ts
      transaction-facade.service.ts
    /categories
      category-facade.service.ts
      category.routes.ts
    /merchants
      merchant-facade.service.ts
      merchant.routes.ts
    /classifications
      classification-facade.service.ts
    /users
      user-facade.service.ts
      user.routes.ts
  /api-client                       <- orval output — DO NOT EDIT MANUALLY
    finance-core.service.ts
    /models
  app.routes.ts
  app.component.ts
  app.config.ts
```

### State Management

- Angular Signals for local and feature-level state (default)
- RxJS for async streams — convert to signals at boundaries
- No NgRx unless cross-feature state complexity justifies it

```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class TransactionFacadeService {
  private readonly api = inject(FinanceCoreService);
  private readonly _transactions = signal<TransactionDto[]>([]);
  readonly transactions = this._transactions.asReadonly();

  loadTransactions(destroyRef: DestroyRef): void {
    this.api.getTransactions()
      .pipe(takeUntilDestroyed(destroyRef))
      .subscribe(result => this._transactions.set(result.data));
  }
}
```

Always pass DestroyRef to any method that subscribes. Never leave subscriptions without teardown.

### Styles

- SCSS for all component styles
- Theme values go in CSS custom properties — no hardcoded colors or sizes in component files
- Global custom properties defined in src/styles.scss

### Error Handling (Frontend)

- error.interceptor.ts catches all API errors
- Parse RFC 7807 ProblemDetails — map status + type to user-friendly messages
- Never display raw detail strings from the API to users

### Anti-Patterns (STRICTLY FORBIDDEN)

- Editing generated API client files manually
- Hardcoded endpoint strings in frontend services
- Duplicated DTO types between frontend and backend
- any in TypeScript
- NgModules (@NgModule)
- Class-based interceptors
- loadChildren with a module — use loadComponent
- Hardcoding apiBaseUrl outside environment.ts
- amount.value / 100 anywhere except MoneyFormatPipe
- Subscriptions without takeUntilDestroyed or equivalent teardown
- Attaching Authorization header in the mutator
- Constructor injection in Angular — use inject()

---

## AI / Classification Layer (INITIAL RULES)

- LLM calls abstracted behind IClassificationProvider in Application/Shared
- Concrete implementations live in Infrastructure
- PII must NOT be sent to external LLM APIs without an explicit data handling decision
- All LLM calls must respect CancellationToken
- Set an explicit HttpClient timeout for LLM calls (recommended: 30s)
- LLM API keys in environment variables only — never hardcoded

---

## Logging

- No Console.Write*
- Use ILogger<T> with structured logging
- Always include context: resource IDs, operation names, caller IDs
- 500 errors: log full exception with LogError
- 4xx errors: do NOT log

---

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Used by |
|---|---|
| DATABASE_URL | Infrastructure (connection string) |
| JWT_SECRET | Api (JWT signing) |
| SWAGGER_URL | Frontend CI (orval input) |
| OPENAI_API_KEY (or equivalent) | Infrastructure (LLM provider) |

