## Testing Conventions

### Backend — xUnit + Moq + FluentAssertions

Test name pattern: should_[action]_[condition]

```csharp
public class GetTransactionByIdQueryHandlerTests
{
    [Fact]
    public async Task should_return_transaction_when_caller_owns_it()
    {
        Mock<ITransactionRepository> repo = new();
        // ...
        result.IsSuccess.Should().BeTrue();
        result.Value!.Id.Should().Be(transactionId);
    }

    [Fact]
    public async Task should_return_forbidden_when_caller_does_not_own_transaction()
    { ... }
}
```

Coverage targets (v1):
- Unit tests: handlers and domain models
- Integration tests: controller endpoints (WebApplicationFactory)
- No e2e in v1

### Frontend — Jest + Angular Testing Library

```typescript
describe('TransactionFacadeService', () => {
  it('should load transactions into signal on success', async () => { ... });
});
```

---

## Git and Branching

- main -> production only (protected, no direct commits)
- dev -> active development
- feature/* or HU-XXX -> feature branches

Conventional Commits:
```
feat: add create-transaction command handler
fix: correct money normalization in Money value object
refactor: extract GetTransactionsByUser into dedicated query
```

---

## What NOT to Generate

- No Node.js or Express code
- No dynamic, implicit types, or any
- No static classes or service locator pattern
- No business logic in Controllers — use MediatR handlers
- No hardcoded secrets or connection strings
- No synchronous/blocking operations where avoidable
- No EF data annotations on domain models
- No decimal, double, float, or int for monetary amounts
- No SaveChanges inside a Repository
- No direct DbContext injection outside Infrastructure
- No generic repository pattern
- No NgModules
- No class-based Angular interceptors
- No constructor injection in Angular — use inject()
- No loadChildren with a module — use loadComponent
- No amount.value / 100 outside MoneyFormatPipe
- No subscriptions without takeUntilDestroyed or equivalent teardown
- No exceptions thrown for business errors — use Result.Failure(Error.X(...))
- No AutoMapper
